  } else {
    // Handle the failure case gracefully in your UI
    console.log('Could not load data. Showing fallback UI.');
  }
})();
```

This pattern gives you:
- A single place to handle network and parsing errors.
- Automatic detection of HTTP failures via `response.ok`.
- A predictable return type (`object` or `null`) so your UI logic can decide what to do when requests fail.

You can later extend this helper (e.g., by adding timeouts, custom headers, or retry logic) without changing call sites across your app.

