To handle multiple asynchronous API requests concurrently in TypeScript, you can use Promises in combination with the `Promise.allSettled` method. This approach allows you to execute all requests in parallel and manage their responses individually, regardless of whether they succeed or fail. Here's how you can implement it:

First, you create a function to simulate an API request. This function returns a promise that randomly resolves or rejects to mimic success and failure scenarios. Then, for each URL in your list, create a promise representing an API request using this function.

By utilizing `Promise.allSettled`, you can run these promises simultaneously, ensuring that all requests are processed without blocking the execution of others. Afterward, you can iterate over the results and handle each response based on its success or failure status, providing individual error handling and response management:

```typescript
// Function to simulate an API request
function simulateApiRequest(url: string): Promise<string> {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        setTimeout(() => {
            if (Math.random() > 0.5) { // Random success or failure
                resolve(`Success: Data from ${url}`);
            } else {
                reject(`Error: Failed to fetch from ${url}`);
            }
        }, Math.random() * 2000);
    });
}

async function fetchConcurrentApis(urls: string[]): Promise<void> {
    const requests = urls.map(url => simulateApiRequest(url));

    // Use Promise.allSettled to handle each request independently
    const results = await Promise.allSettled(requests);

    results.forEach((result, index) => {
        if (result.status === 'fulfilled') {
            console.log(`Request to ${urls[index]} succeeded with response:`, result.value);
        } else {
            console.error(`Request to ${urls[index]} failed with error:`, result.reason);
        }
    });
}

// Example usage
const urls = [
    'https://api.example.com/endpoint1',
    'https://api.example.com/endpoint2',
    'https://api.example.com/endpoint3'
];

fetchConcurrentApis(urls).catch(error => console.error('Unexpected error:', error));
