const validationErrors = incomingUser.validateProfile();

if (validationErrors.length > 0) {
  console.log('Cannot persist user record. Validation errors:', validationErrors);
} else {
  console.log('User entity is valid and ready for persistence:', incomingUser);
}
```

This design:
- Uses a generated UUID to ensure each user record is uniquely identifiable, even before database insertion.
- Leverages TypeScript’s optional properties (`email?`, `age?`) to reflect that some fields may be missing or filled later.
